RUF051 [*] Use `pop` instead of `key in dict` followed by `del dict[key]`
  --> RUF051.py:8:5
   |
 7 | if k in d:                          # Bare name
 8 |     del d[k]
   |     ^^^^^^^^
 9 |
10 | if '' in d:                         # String
   |
help: Replace `if` statement with `.pop(..., None)`
  |
7 - if k in d:                          # Bare name
8 -     del d[k]
7 + d.pop(k, None)
  |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

